| Surface | GitHub repo | Local path | Required branch |
|---|---|---|---|
| WEBSITE | `streamerstipReact` | `/Users/tristanmartin/Projects/streamerstipReact` | `homepage-merge-staging` |
| FLUTTER APP | `flutterStreamersTip2` | `/Users/tristanmartin/Projects/flutterST` | `flutterStreamersTip2` |

`flutterST` is the local folder for GitHub `flutterStreamersTip2` on branch `flutterStreamersTip2`. Folder name, GitHub name, and branch name are **one checkout**, not three codebases. Do not treat this folder as a patches/drop-pack repo, and do not move implementation work to a different clone because of the folder name.

## Before any code change

Run and report:

```bash
git rev-parse --show-toplevel
git branch --show-current
git status --short
```

Stop unless this workspace is `/Users/tristanmartin/Projects/flutterST` on `flutterStreamersTip2`. If required code is not on this branch, stop and report what is missing. Do not restore code from another branch.

## Never without explicit user approval

- `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git worktree`, or any command that changes branches
- Creating a new branch
- Switching because related StreamersTip code exists elsewhere
- Modifying `/Users/tristanmartin/Projects/streamerstipReact` during Flutter work

A task that mentions another repo/branch is **not** authorization to switch to it.

If a branch change seems necessary, stop and report: current repo, current branch, needed branch, why. Wait for explicit approval.

Website and Flutter must share the same canonical Firestore contracts, but they remain separate repositories.
